 # Mesh Topology and Robust Digitization
 ## Overview
-This family of methods converts polygon meshes into discrete volumetric representations (voxel grids) while prioritizing topological validity and robustness against geometric defects [G]. Unlike standard rasterization which may produce gaps or artifacts on non-watertight or low-quality meshes, these techniques enforce structural integrity, ensuring the resulting volume accurately reflects the mesh's interior or surface connectivity [G]. They differ from primitive-based union methods by treating the mesh as a unified solid object rather than a collection of independent bounding volumes [4605-polygon-mesh-voxelization-via-union-of-sets.md].
